    <DataNode elementId="AT2G37250-MONOMER" textLabel="Adenylate kinase 1, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9ZUU1" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="475" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The enzyme catalyzing the reversible transphosphorylation reaction that interconverts ADP to ATP and AMP, i.e. adenylate kinase has been identified and characterized in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The enzyme is located in the chloroplast as demonstrated by both cellular fractionation and green fluorescent protein (GFP) localization experiments |CITS: [15618410]|.</Comment>
